{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ShdDoqCVso44Y8ToDQWaJ3","type":"tool_result","content":"d01_analysis_section_names :: For the bundled Day 1 ELF, submit the section names in section-header-table order as a JSON array of strings. The mandatory null section at index 0 has an empty name; including or omitting that one leading empty string is accepted. Do not substitute the section type NULL for its empty name. \n {\"kind\": \"json\", \"syntax\": \"JSON array of section-name strings in section-header-table order; an optional leading empty string represents section index 0\"} \n\nd01_analysis_disassembly :: In the bundled Day 1 ELF, find the recover_code FUNC symbol in the symbol table and disassemble its bytes. Submit its decoded instructions in execution order as a JSON array of strings, without addresses or byte columns. If that symbol is absent, submit []. Unrelated format example: [\"nop\",\"ret\"]. \n {\"kind\": \"json\", \"syntax\": \"JSON array of instruction strings in execution order; an empty array if the recover_code symbol is absent. Intel or AT&T spelling of the same constant-return instructions is accepted.\"} \n\nd03_analysis_format :: For the bundled Day 3 managed binary, identify its combined executable-container and managed-runtime format classification. Submit one compound token containing both parts, not just the generic container label. A tool-specific container label such as a bitness-qualified form is accepted when it identifies the same container. Unrelated syntax example: sample_vm. \n {\"kind\": \"pattern\", \"syntax\": \"one container_runtime token; PE, PE32, or PE32+ may name the same container and CLI, CLR, or .NET may name the managed part; underscore, slash, hyphen, or space separators and letter case are accepted\"} \n\nd06_analysis_compression_methods :: For the requested JAR, submit the distinct ZIP compression methods used by every central-directory entry, including directory entries, as a JSON array. Numeric ZIP method codes or their standard Stored/Deflate names are accepted; order and duplicate observations do not matter. \n {\"kind\": \"json\", \"syntax\": \"JSON array of distinct ZIP compression method codes or standard method names across all file and directory entries\"} \n\nd08_analysis_format :: For the requested specimen in the bundled archive, identify its executable container from the final bytes. Submit an ELF or PE container label; letter case and a more specific ELF32, ELF64, PE32, PE32+, or Portable Executable label are accepted when they identify the same container. \n {\"kind\": \"pattern\", \"syntax\": \"ELF or PE executable-container label; bitness-qualified standard labels and letter-case differences are accepted\"}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41c40dd5-eb72-4691-b80c-2f2f7cef8026","uuid":"d1d5b225-3034-4e7c-8704-3efdb9583698","timestamp":"2026-10-17T17:10:06.798Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"d01_analysis_section_names :: For the bundled Day 1 ELF, submit the section names in section-header-table order as a JSON array of strings. The mandatory null section at index 0 has an empty name; including or omitting that one leading empty string is accepted. Do not substitute the section type NULL for its empty name. \n {\"kind\": \"json\", \"syntax\": \"JSON array of section-name strings in section-header-table order; an optional leading empty string represents section index 0\"} \n\nd01_analysis_disassembly :: In the bundled Day 1 ELF, find the recover_code FUNC symbol in the symbol table and disassemble its bytes. Submit its decoded instructions in execution order as a JSON array of strings, without addresses or byte columns. If that symbol is absent, submit []. Unrelated format example: [\"nop\",\"ret\"]. \n {\"kind\": \"json\", \"syntax\": \"JSON array of instruction strings in execution order; an empty array if the recover_code symbol is absent. Intel or AT&T spelling of the same constant-return instructi