[I] pyelftools; `readelf -SW f; readelf -sW f` | high |\n103\t| 63 | Build provenance: GNU build-id, `.comment` compiler banner, Go buildinfo, rustc commit, PE timestamp/Rich/PDB | gap (Go buildinfo used internally) | `.note.gnu.build-id` (20-byte SHA1), `GCC: (Debian 15...)`, `go1.NN`, `/rustc/<sha>`, `TimeDateStamp`, RSDS | [I] `readelf -nW f`; `readelf -p .comment f`; `go version -m f`; `pefile` `FILE_HEADER.TimeDateStamp` | med (natural \"compiler/language\" id; label spelling unknown) |\n104\t| 64 | Demangling + C++ vtable/typeinfo | seen D2, D8 (has_cpp_*) | `_Z`, `_ZTV`, `$s` Swift, `_D` D, Nim `__mod_u`, Rust `_R`/`17h..E` | [I] `c++filt`, `rustfilt`, `swift-demangle`, `nim-demangle`, `llvm-cxxfilt-18`; GM wants MANGLED form | high (carry-over) |\n105\t| 65 | File hashes beyond sha256 (imphash, ssdeep, TLSH, md5) | gap | id names like `imphash`/`ssdeep`; only sha256 asked so far | [I] python `pefile` `get_imphash()`, `md5sum`; [M] ssdeep/tlsh python | low |\n106\t| 66 | Same-source build PAIR, qualifier ids `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` | seen D15 (stripped/symbolized), D16 (compact/direct) | two `dNN--variant-XXX-<tag>.<ext>` members, near-identical sizes, same HCFG; sha256_K = archive order (reverse-alpha both days); config asked for one tag only | [I] solver `_qualified` router (file-name token -> member; structural fallback) | med-high (D15-D16 pairs, D17 broke the streak; D17 backfill asked config ids for the other tag too; next tags: static/dynamic, O0/O2, pie/nopie, packed/unpacked, x86_64/aarch64) |\n107\t| 67 | WASM \"doors\" inventory: imports, exports, memory limits, table/elem (`call_indirect`), start, globals, custom `name`/`producers` | gap (D16 prompt theme; unasked) | import section id 2 (`env.*`/`wasi_snapshot_preview1.*`), table id 4, elem id 9, `call_indirect` 0x11 | [I] `wasm-objdump -x -j Import -j Export -j Table -j Elem f`; extend `lib.binary.wasm_layout` | high (prebuilt wasm-inventory-fields; the D17 backfill pattern = old days' themes get asked later on their group) |\n108\t| 68 | WASM from real toolchains (Emscripten, wasi-sdk/clang, Rust, Go, AssemblyScript), memory64, passive segments, HCFG in custom section / split / i32.store-built | gap | `global.get __memory_base` init expr, `memory.init` 0xfc 08, `producers` section, AssemblyScript UTF-16 strings, Go `go:buildid` | [I] `wasm2wat`, `wasm-decompile`; `hcfg_scan` (utf16) ; clang-18 `--target=wasm32-wasi -c` (object only: no wasm-ld) | med |\n109\t| 69 | eBPF object (ELF e_machine 247) | gap | ELF64 ET_REL, sections `license`, `.maps`, `xdp`/`kprobe/...`/`tracepoint/...`, `.BTF`/`.BTF.ext` | [I] `readelf -hSW f.o` (machine \"Linux BPF\"); `llvm-objdump-18 -d f.o`; `clang-18 -target bpf -c` builds fixtures | med (natural \"sandboxed code\" sequel to WASM) |\n110\t| 70 | Bytecode containers: LLVM bitcode, Python `.pyc`, Lua `luac`, standalone `.class`/`.dex` | gap | `BC\\xc0\\xde` / wrapper `de c0 17 0b`; pyc magic `xx 0d 0d 0a`; `\\x1bLua`; `CAFEBABE` major>=45; `dex\\n035` | [I] `llvm-dis-18`/`llvm-bcanalyzer-18`; `pycdas`; `luac -l -l`; `javap`; jadx | low-med (format label unknown -> submit alone) |\n111\t| 71 | Section-less / corrupted ELF headers (sstrip, e_shnum 0, bogus e_shoff/e_shstrndx) | gap | `readelf -S`: \"There are no sections\", pyelftools exceptions, PT_LOAD only | [I] `readelf -lW f`; parse program headers; `rz-bin -I f`; HCFG via raw scan | med (next escalation of \"Stripped\") |\n112\t| 72 | Backfill of an earlier day's single-solve facts on its old group | seen D8 (pad to 10), **D17** (pad to 11: marker, recover_code, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_coroutine_runtime) | ids on dNN groups that the solver's field table does not know; generic `field N` wording | [I] per-language facts dict in the solver; `javap -v -p`, `nm`, `readelf -sW`, `GoReSym` | high (next backfill likely reaches D8-D17 facts: swift5 sections/protocols, Nim/D/Crystal runtimes, Zig/FPC/ObjC class+selector lists, pair diffs, wasm exports, Ada GNAT) |\n113\t| 73 | `hcfg_storage` label (how the blob is stored) | **seen D17** (exact_text on d08/d09/d11-d14) | base64 `SENGR` literal vs raw `HCFG` | `base64` GM-confirmed; RAW word UNKNOWN (~117 spellings rejected, list in the technique log) | high (re-asked every backfill day; never batch the raw ones) |\n114\t| 74 | Config decoder routine as answer (algorithm, key, function name, loop shape) | gap (D17 prompt \"recover the reversible decoder\", unasked) | function xrefing the stored blob; `xor byte [..], imm8` / `xor al, 0x73` loops; Ada `pkg__decode_config` | [I] capstone over the function referencing the blob VA; `rizin -q -c 'aaa; axt @ <blob va>' f` | med (theme may be backfilled on d17 later) |\n115\t\n116\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n117\t```\n118\tSTEP 1  file -b F ; xxd -l 64 F            -> container + arch + stripped/static/PIE in one line\n119\t  7f454c46 ELF: byte4 1=ELF32 2=ELF64; byte5 1=LE 2=BE (BE => read e_machine/HCFG ints big-endian)\n120\t  4d5a MZ->PE: Machine 0x14c i386 | 0x8664 x86-64 | 0xaa64 AArch64 | 0x1c0/0x1c4 ARM; \"Mono/.Net\" => pe_cli\n121\t  cffaedfe/cefaedfe Mach-O thin; cafebabe + small u32 nfat => Mach-O FAT (NOT a Java class) ; format word presumed `macho`\n122\t  504b0304 zip/jar/apk (keep nested jars whole) ; 1b4c7561 Lua ; 1b4c4a LuaJIT ; FOR1..BEAM Erlang ; 4243c0de LLVM bitcode\n123\t  0061736d \\0asm WASM (D16): format `wasm`, architecture `wasm32` (GM-confirmed); lib.binary.wasm_layout -> sections, memories,\n124\t    data_segments (file_offset + mem_offset); wasm-objdump -x F ; HCFG RAW in data seg 0 -> raw scan finds it (crc-gate)\n125\t  ':10' text lines => Intel HEX ; 'S0'/'S1' => S-record ; no magic + ARM vector table => raw firmware (rizin -m base)\n126\tSTEP 2  rz-bin -I F   (or readelf -hlSW F)  -> lang, machine, bits, endian, static, stripped, pic, relro, nx, canary\n127\t  e_machine: 3 x86 | 62 x86-64 | 40 ARM | 183 AArch64 | 8 MIPS | 20 PPC | 21 PPC64 | 243 RISC-V | 2/43 SPARC\n128\t  labels: GM-confirmed x86-64/x86/AArch64/ARM (ELF), i386/x86-64 (PE); others = readelf spelling first, then EM_ name minus\n129\t  prefix; kind:integer => decimal e_machine. Dispatch on answer_format.kind, never on field name.\n130\t  no .symtab => stripped (answer [] / none / false); no INTERP => static; ET_DYN+INTERP => PIE; ET_REL => object file\n131\t  UPX0/UPX1 sections or \"UPX!\" or entropy>7.2 => PACKED: upx -t F; cp F /tmp/x; upx -d /tmp/x (fix zeroed UPX! first)\n132\tSTEP 3  strings -a -n6 F | grep -m8 -E 'GCC:|clang|rustc|go1\\.|GHC |OCaml|caml_|FPC |Crystal|zig|GNAT Version|gfortran|DMD|Nim|\n133\t        swift|_kDart|kfun:|__svm|MEI|nuitka|AU3!|Borland|MSVBVM|libcob|UPX|HCFG|SENGR'   -> toolchain + blob form\n134\t  toolchain -> tool: Go GoReSym -t -d -p | Rust rustfilt | .NET ilspycmd | jar javap -v -p / jadx | Swift swift-demangle\n135\t  Nim nim-demangle | PyInstaller pyinstxtractor+pycdc | AutoIt autoit-ripper | anything else: rizin -q -c 'aaa;afl' /\n136\t  analyzeHeadless (lib.binary.ghidra_decompile) | foreign arch: rizin -a <arch> / llvm-objdump-18 / Ghidra (no exec, qemu absent)\n137\tHCFG (every new member since D2)\n138\t  python: from lib.binary import hcfg_find, hcfg_scan; hcfg_find(open(F,'rb').read())  -> config, offset, encoding, key, crc_ok\n139\t  raw magic 'HCFG' | b64 'SENGR' | hex '48434647' | rot13 'FRATE' | b64-zlib 'eJ' | b64-gzip 'H4sI' -> covered by hcfg_scan\n140\t  accept only crc32(plain)==header crc AND JSON parses; keep scanning past decoys (D9 had two raw-magic decoys)\n141\t  NOT FOUND => blob is hidden: (1) packed? unpack; (2) AES S-box 637c777b / TEA 9e3779b9 / 'expand 32-byte k' => find key+IV\n142\t  near the call, decrypt with pycryptodome; (3) runs of mov [rbp-x], imm => stack-built: collect imms with capstone or\n143\t  emulate the builder with unicorn; (4) PE .rsrc / .NET resource / jar non-class entry / overlay past last section;\n144\t  (5) .init_array / TLS callback decoder => emulate it. Offsets: raw=the H, base64=the S (GM-confirmed); else first stored byte.\n145\tFIELDS: format = container only (elf/pe/macho?/jar; .NET pe_cli) | machine/architecture = container machine word |\n146\t  qualifier ids dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field> -> member whose file name has <tag> (D15 stripped/symbolized, D16 compact/direct;\n147\t  match the LONGEST member-name token, a tag may contain `_`) ; sha256_K = zip archive order | config_* verbatim from HCFG JSON |\n148\t  has_<x>_section = literal section name | hex fields lowercase 0x | never chase the prompt's theme: answer only asked ids.\n149\t  D17 Ada ELF (GNAT 14.2): plain ELF, HCFG RAW in .rodata -> carried-over solver answers it unchanged.\n150\tBACKFILL ids on OLD groups (D8, D17): an unknown field on dNN = that day's own facts. Seen: marker (.huntress string),\n151\t  recover_code (decimal imm), mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol (bare _ZNK.../_ZTI...; PE .text$/.rdata$), has_go_runtime,\n152\t  has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime (enum true/false), methods (Main-Class method_info names incl <init>, JSON),\n153\t  access_flags (decimal, 49), method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>). Derive from bytes, POST all derivable ones together.\n154\thcfg_storage: base64 literal -> `base64` (GM). RAW -> unknown word: send ALONE, cap ~10 probes, then HELP; never batch it.\n155\t```\n156\t\n157\t## Readiness gaps\n158\t```json\n159\t[\n160\t  {\"id\": \"backfill-language-identity-facts\", \"concept\": \"Per-language identity + theme facts for the D8-D17 groups (the next backfill): has_<lang>_runtime / has_<lang>_mangled_symbol / class, protocol, selector, proc, template names\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 re-asked D1-D7's single-solve facts on their old groups (marker, recover_code, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_coroutine_runtime). Build ONE generic facts table so the D8-D17 analogues answer without code: has_swift_runtime (swift5_* sections / `$s` symbols), has_nim_runtime (NimMain), has_zig_runtime (.comment zig / `std.` panic strings), has_d_runtime (`_D4core`/`_D2rt`), has_fpc_runtime (FPC banner / `.fpcdata`), has_crystal_runtime (`Crystal:H`/`*crystal*`), has_objc_runtime (`__objc_*` sections, objc_msg_lookup), has_gnat_runtime (`GNAT Version`, `__gnat_`), has_wasm_*; plus name lists: ObjC classes/selectors (`._OBJC_CLASS_`, `objc_sel_name_`), Swift type/protocol names (demangled `$s` nominal types), Nim procs (`<proc>__<mod>_u<N>`), D functions (`_D<len>`), Ada subprograms (`pkg__sub`), mangled forms kept (GM wants MANGLED). Fixtures: the cached real members from day08-day17 single_solve/work/extracted (bytes on disk) + expected values in a table; every field returns `none`/`false` on absence, never raises.\"},\n161\t  {\"id\": \"jvm-classfile-facts\", \"concept\": \"Full JVM ClassFile facts for jar groups (d06/d07): versions, constant-pool count, this/super/interfaces, fields, methods+descriptors, attributes, Kotlin metadata\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 asked methods (names, table order, incl <init>), access_flags (decimal 49) and method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>) of the Main-Class. Next backfill may ask major_version/minor_version, constant_pool_count, super_class, interfaces, field names/count, method descriptors, SourceFile attribute, main_class (Manifest), class_count/entry_count, Kotlin `@Metadata` d1/d2, invokeSuspend label states. Implement a stdlib ClassFile parser in lib (javap -v -p parity tests on fixture jars built with javac/kotlinc-free hand-made classes); JSON compact, table order, decimal ints.\"},\n162\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-metadata-facts\", \"concept\": \".NET metadata facts for the d03 group: assembly name/version, MVID, TypeDef/MethodDef names, FieldRVA, TargetFramework, entry point token\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"d03 is the only old group whose day-facts were not re-asked on D17 (it got hcfg_version/xor_key_hex only); a later backfill likely asks typedef/method names, method_count, assembly_name, assembly_version, target_framework (runtimeconfig tfm), entry_point token hex, has_field_rva. Use dnfile (installed) + ilspycmd parity on a dotnet-built fixture dll; JSON lists in table order, `<Module>` and `<PrivateImplementationDetails>` kept as named.\"},\n163\t  {\"id\": \"decoder-routine-locator\", \"concept\": \"Locate and characterise the config DECODER in the binary: function name, algorithm (xor/add/rol/rc4...), key/immediate, loop length, references to the stored blob\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 prompt: 'Recover the reversible decoder' (unasked, but a later backfill may ask decoder facts on d17 or any HCFG group). From the validated HcfgHit: compute blob VA, find code xrefs (RIP-relative lea/mov to VA in .text via capstone, or rizin `axt`), report the containing FUNC symbol (Ada `pkg__decode_config`, Nim/D/Crystal mangled kept), the xor immediate(s) inside the loop and whether it equals header key; return algorithm token `xor` speculative. Fixtures: gcc -O0/-O2 C decoders (xor, add, rol, rolling) with symbols and stripped.\"},\n164\t  {\"id\": \"native-imports-exports-facts\", \"concept\": \"imports / NEEDED / interpreter / exports lists for ELF, PE, Mach-O\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Generic facts: ELF `needed` (DT_NEEDED order), `imports` (UND .dynsym names, table order, version suffix stripped), `interpreter` (.interp without NUL), `exports` (defined dynsyms); PE import dll list + functions (`dll!func`?), exports, imphash; Mach-O LC_LOAD_DYLIB. JSON compact like symbols. D15 symbolized had getenv/strcmp/printf, unasked. D17 backfill pattern (old days re-asked as per-group facts) makes imports/NEEDED lists a likely next field on any native group.\"},\n165\t  {\"id\": \"provenance-facts-extractor\", \"concept\": \"Build provenance fields: GNU build-id, .comment compiler banner, DWARF producer/language/comp_dir, PE TimeDateStamp/PDB path/Rich, Go/Rust toolchain version\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Implement in the facts dict so a new id answers without code: build_id = lowercase hex of NT_GNU_BUILD_ID desc (no 0x), compiler = first `.comment` string, dwarf_producer via pyelftools, pdb_path from RSDS, timestamp as int and ISO. Fixtures from the existing TARGETS.json builds (gcc -g, -Wl,--build-id). Spellings unknown -> submit alone. D17 member had DWARF (Ada, producer `GNU Ada 14.2.0`): dwarf_language/producer is a plausible backfill id for d05/d11/d17.\"},\n166\t  {\"id\": \"hcfg-storage-raw-label\", \"concept\": \"GM word for a RAW-stored HCFG in `hcfg_storage` (d12 FPC .data, d14 ObjC .hcfg)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D17: `base64` confirmed for SENGR literals; ~117 raw spellings rejected (raw, plain, bytes, binary, blob, xor, section, data, .data, .hcfg, rodata, struct, literal, inline, embedded, none, base64 and combos -- full list in the technique log). Untried: hex, encoded, xor_encoded, obfuscated, magic, header, framed, typed_const, array_of_byte, c_array, uint8_array, objc_section, fpc_data. When re-asked: submit raw ids ALONE after everything else banked, cap ~10 probes, then HELP; ask the organizers if a hint channel exists. Never let it hold the other ids.\"},\n167\t  {\"id\": \"language-detector\", \"concept\": \"lib.binary.language_of(data) -> source language/toolchain token with evidence, for all 17 seen languages + next candidates\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A `language`/`compiler`/`toolchain` id on any group would need consistent tokens: c, cpp, csharp/dotnet, go, rust, java, kotlin, swift, nim, zig, d, pascal/fpc, crystal, objc, wat/wasm, ada; candidates haskell, ocaml, fortran, cobol, odin, v, dart, julia, kotlin-native, python(pyinstaller/nuitka). Cue table = atlas STEP 3 regex + section/symbol markers; verify on every cached dNN member (expected = the day's language), log ambiguity rather than guess.\"},\n168\t  {\"id\": \"emulate-return-value\", \"concept\": \"Recover a function's return value by emulation when it is not a `mov eax, imm; ret` leaf (obfuscated/computed/OLLVM recover_code)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"recover_code was re-asked D17; a mutated variant may compute the constant (xor of two imms, lookup table, flattened switch). unicorn x86-64 (installed): map the ELF PT_LOADs, set rsp to a scratch stack, run from the FUNC symbol until ret with an instruction cap, read eax; refuse on syscalls/calls into libc. Fixtures: gcc -O0/-O2 builds with arithmetic-constant and table-lookup returns; AArch64 via unicorn ARM64 for the cross-arch case.\"},"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41c40dd5-eb72-4691-b80c-2f2f7cef8026","uuid":"f123fcc5-9e89-42a4-b812-d6177992998b","timestamp":"2026-10-17T17:10:27.768Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md","content":"# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D17, 2026-10-17)\n\nScope: what a D18+ `evidence.zip` group (or backfilled old-group id) could be, how we would recognise it, which standard tool answers it, and how ready we\nare. Grounded in `reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` (lane log D1-D17), `challenges/day17/binary-decoder-ring/solver/`,\n`lib/binary.py` (`hcfg_scan`/`hcfg_find`, `packer_info`, `unpack_upx`, `go_buildinfo`, `go_pclntab_funcs`, `rustfilt`, `macho_facts`,\n`recover_return_constants`, `ghidra_decompile`, `jar_app_classes`, `wasm_layout`) and `tests/data/binary_fixtures/TARGETS.json` (all 9 targets have fixtures).\n\nProgression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\nlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix from the file-name tag (C ELF\n`stripped`/`symbolized`; WebAssembly `compact`/`direct`, labels `wasm`/`wasm32`); D17 \"Decoder Ring\" = back to ONE new language\n(Ada/GNAT ELF, HCFG RAW in `.rodata`, nothing new to decode) + BACKFILL #2 (160 -> 204 ids, 11 per old group) that re-asked\nEARLIER DAYS' single-solve facts (d01 marker/recover_code, d02 mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol, d04 has_go_runtime, d05\nhas_rust_mangled_symbol, d06 methods/access_flags, d07 method_count/has_coroutine_runtime) and a NEW label field `hcfg_storage`\n(`base64` confirmed; the RAW-storage word was never found in ~117 POSTs). Lessons for D18+: (a) the next backfill will most likely\nreach D8-D17's own day facts (Swift/Nim/Zig/D/FPC/Crystal/ObjC/pair/wasm/Ada identity booleans, symbol names, class/selector\nlists, wasm imports/exports) -- the \"theme\" of a day is answerable LATER on its old group; (b) the new-day member keeps being a\nplain ELF whose ids the carried-over solver already answers (D17 group banked at T+18 s); (c) label fields with no derivable\nspelling (`hcfg_storage` raw, D3 `pe_cli`) are the real time sink. Asked field names: config_*, format, machine, architecture,\nelf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols, section_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*,\nhas_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags,\nmethod_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset, hcfg_version, hcfg_storage, xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods.\nRemaining risks: (1) more per-language fact backfills, (2) a twist that hides the HCFG from a byte scan (the D17 \"decoder\" theme\ndid not materialise but stays plausible: packing, real crypto, stack-built, per-string encryption, API hashing), (3) a new\ncontainer/arch label (Mach-O, eBPF, AArch64...), (4) more pair days with `_`-containing tags.\n\nTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\nInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\nllvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\nrizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\nAARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\njadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara, wabt (wasm-objdump/wasm2wat/wat2wasm/wasm-decompile), floss (.venv), luac,\n7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\nlz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only).\nMissing: qemu-user(-static), wasm-ld/lld, wasmtime, capa, Detect-It-Easy (diec), de4dot, monodis, erlang (beam_disasm),\nunluac/luajit-decompiler (luac present), blutter, srecord (srec_cat), binutils-multiarch, checksec, python zstandard/brotli, rzpipe/r2pipe.\n\n## Concept table\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D18+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | C ELF (gcc, glibc) | seen D1, D15 (+ every day's d01; D17 re-asked marker/recover_code) | `GCC: (...)` in `.comment`, `.interp` ld-linux, `__libc_start_main` | [I] `readelf -hSW f; readelf -sW f; objdump -d -M intel f` | high (carry-over every day; mastery d01 re-rolls stripped/renamed) |\n| 2 | C++ Itanium ELF / MinGW PE32+ | seen D2 | `_Z` symbols, `_ZTV`/`_ZTI`/`_ZTS`, `libstdc++`; PE `.text$_Z...` COMDAT, `.CRT`, `.tls` | [I] `nm -C f`; `objdump -t f.exe`; `c++filt` | high (carry-over; ELF/PE re-rolls per member) |\n| 3 | .NET C# PE (pe_cli) | seen D3 | `BSJB` metadata root `v4.0.30319`, `mscoree.dll`/`_CorExeMain`, `.runtimeconfig.json` | [I] `ilspycmd f.dll`; python `dnfile` | high (carry-over) |\n| 4 | Go (static, stripped; PE in Mastery) | seen D4 | `\\xff Go buildinf:`, `.gopclntab`, `runtime.`, `go1.NN` | [I] `GoReSym -t -d -p f`; `go version -m f`; `lib.binary.go_buildinfo` | high (carry-over) |\n| 5 | Rust ELF (debug_info) | seen D5 | `_ZN...17h<16hex>E` / `_R` v0 symbols, `rustc version`, `/rustc/<sha>/library` panic paths | [I] `rustfilt < syms`; `readelf -p .comment f` | high (carry-over) |\n| 6 | Rust stripped / release | gap | no `.symtab`, panic strings + `/rustc/<40hex>/` paths remain, `core::fmt` strings | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep -m3 /rustc/`; Ghidra headless; [M] no cargo-rustc symbol-recovery tool | med (natural \"stripped\" sequel for any language) |\n| 7 | Java / Kotlin jar | seen D6, D7 (D17 re-asked methods/access_flags/method_count/has_coroutine_runtime) | `PK` + `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF`, `CAFEBABE` classes, `kotlin/` packages | [I] `unzip -l f.jar; javap -v -p -c Main.class`; `jadx -d out f.jar`; `lib.binary.jar_app_classes` | high (carry-over) |\n| 8 | Swift ELF (static stdlib, 67 MB) | seen D8 | `swift5_*` sections, `$s` symbols, `libswiftCore` | [I] `bin/swift-demangle`; regex `SENGR` in `.rodata` | high (carry-over) |\n| 9 | Nim / D / Crystal ELF | seen D9, D11, D13 | Nim `NimMain`,`fatal.nim`; D `_D4core`,`DMDH`; Crystal `Crystal:H`,`GC_malloc` | [I] `bin/nim-demangle`; `grep -abo 'SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/=]*' f` | high (carry-over) |\n| 10 | Zig ELF + PE | seen D10 | `.comment` \"zig-bootstrap\"/LLD 19, stripped, `.hcfg` section | [I] `readelf -p .comment f; readelf -x .hcfg f` | high (carry-over) |\n| 11 | Free Pascal ELF | seen D12 | `FPC 3.2.2`, `.fpcdata`, `FPC_` symbols, static stripped | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep FPC`; `grep -abo HCFG f` | high (carry-over) |\n| 12 | Objective-C (GNUstep) ELF | seen D14 | `__objc_selectors`/`__objc_classes`, `objc_msg_lookup`, `._OBJC_CLASS_` | [I] `readelf -sW f \\| grep -E '_OBJC_CLASS_\\|objc_sel_name_'` | high (carry-over) |\n| 13 | Haskell (GHC) | gap | `hs_main`, `ghczmprim_`/`base_GHCziBase` z-encoded symbols, `GHC <ver>` rts strings, huge static ELF | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep -m2 'GHC '`; `nm f \\| grep -c _info$`; [M] no hsdecomp | med (classic \"weird runtime\" language left on the list) |\n| 14 | OCaml native | gap | `caml_startup`, `camlStdlib__`, `caml_main`, `OCAMLRUNPARAM` | [I] `nm f \\| grep -m5 '^.* T caml'`; `strings -a f \\| grep -i ocaml` | med |\n| 15 | V language | gap | `main__main`, `v__`/`builtin__` symbols, compiled via C (`.comment` GCC/tcc) | [I] `nm f \\| grep -E 'main__main\\|builtin__'` | low-med |\n| 16 | Dart AOT (`dart compile exe`) / Flutter `libapp.so` | gap | `_kDartVmSnapshotData`/`_kDartIsolateSnapshotInstructions` symbols, `Dart_` strings, snapshot hash | [I] `readelf -sW f \\| grep _kDart`; [M] blutter (`github.com/worawit/blutter`) | low-med (snapshot strings are compressed: HCFG may not be byte-visible) |\n| 17 | Fortran (gfortran) | gap | `_gfortran_` imports, `MAIN__`, `libgfortran.so.5` NEEDED | [I] `readelf -dW f \\| grep NEEDED`; `nm -D f \\| grep gfortran` | med (pun-friendly title, trivial for organizers) |\n| 18 | Ada (GNAT) | **seen D17** (1.4 MB dynamic ELF, GNAT 14.2.0, not stripped, DWARF) | `GNAT Version: 14.2.0`, `ada__*`/`system__*`/`__gnat_*` symbols, `ADA.STRINGS.*_ERROR`, `.gcc_except_table`; HCFG RAW in `.rodata` | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep -m1 'GNAT Version'`; `grep -abo HCFG f` (crc-gate); Ada names `pkg__sub` -> `pkg.sub`; [M] gnat (no fixture builds) | high (carry-over; a backfill may ask `has_gnat_runtime`/decoder facts) |\n| 19 | Erlang/Elixir BEAM | gap | `FOR1....BEAM` IFF chunks (`AtU8`,`Code`,`LitT` zlib), escript `#!` + zip | [M] `erl -noshell -eval 'beam_lib:chunks(...)'` (apt erlang-base); [I] python `zlib` on `LitT` | low-med (would be a new container: format label unknown) |\n| 20 | Heavy AOT runtimes: Julia, GraalVM native-image, Kotlin/Native | gap | Julia `libjulia`, `jl_`; GraalVM `__svm_`, `com.oracle.svm`; K/N `kfun:`, `Konan_` | [I] `nm f \\| grep -m5 -E 'kfun:\\|__svm\\|jl_'`; `strings -a f` | low-med (K/N most likely: Kotlin already a theme) |\n| 21 | Python frozen: PyInstaller / Nuitka / py2exe | gap (tooled) | PyInstaller cookie `MEI\\x0c\\x0b\\x0a\\x0b\\x0e`, `pydata` section, `_MEIPASS`; Nuitka `__nuitka`, `NUITKA_ONEFILE`; py2exe `PYTHONSCRIPT` resource | [I] `bin/pyinstxtractor f; bin/pycdc x.pyc`; Nuitka: `strings -a f` + constants blob; [I] `uncompyle6`/`decompyle3` | med (blurs into script lane; HCFG would sit in a marshalled const) |\n| 22 | Lua / LuaJIT bytecode | gap | `\\x1bLua` + version 0x51-0x54; `\\x1bLJ` (LuaJIT); embedded in a C host | [I] `xxd -l 16 f`; [M] `luac -l -l` (apt lua5.4), unluac jar, luajit-decompiler-v2 | low-med |\n| 23 | Legacy Windows: Delphi, VB6, AutoIt | gap (AutoIt tooled) | Delphi `Borland`/`Embarcadero`, `DVCLAL`, `PACKAGEINFO` RCDATA; VB6 `MSVBVM60.DLL`, `VB5!`; AutoIt `AU3!EA06`, RCDATA `SCRIPT` | [I] `bin/autoit-ripper f.exe out/`; python `pefile` resources; [M] IDR/DIE | low (lane is Linux-first; Pascal already done via FPC) |\n| 24 | Niche native langs: Odin, Hare, Vala, GnuCOBOL, Chapel | gap | Odin `runtime.`/`__$startup_runtime`; Vala `g_object_`/GLib; COBOL `cob_init`, `libcob` | [I] `readelf -dW f \\| grep NEEDED`; `nm f \\| head` | med (the organizers clearly have a \"one more language\" list) |\n| 25 | MSVC PE (vs MinGW) | gap (MinGW seen D2) | `Rich`/`DanS` header, `.text$mn`, debug dir RSDS + `.pdb` path, `VCRUNTIME140.dll` | [I] `objdump -x f.exe`; python `pefile` (`RICH_HEADER`, `DIRECTORY_ENTRY_DEBUG`) | low-med |\n| 26 | musl / static linking | seen D4, D5, D8, D12 (static); musl gap | no `.interp`, no `.dynamic`; musl: no `GLIBC_2.` version strings, `__libc_start_main` absent | [I] `readelf -lW f \\| grep -c INTERP`; `strings -a f \\| grep -c GLIBC_` | med (cheap twist \"Static\") |\n| 27 | Mach-O