next escalation of \"Stripped\") |\n| 72 | Backfill of an earlier day's single-solve facts on its old group | seen D8 (pad to 10), **D17** (pad to 11: marker, recover_code, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_coroutine_runtime) | ids on dNN groups that the solver's field table does not know; generic `field N` wording | [I] per-language facts dict in the solver; `javap -v -p`, `nm`, `readelf -sW`, `GoReSym` | high (next backfill likely reaches D8-D17 facts: swift5 sections/protocols, Nim/D/Crystal runtimes, Zig/FPC/ObjC class+selector lists, pair diffs, wasm exports, Ada GNAT) |\n| 73 | `hcfg_storage` label (how the blob is stored) | **seen D17** (exact_text on d08/d09/d11-d14) | base64 `SENGR` literal vs raw `HCFG` | `base64` GM-confirmed; RAW word UNKNOWN (~117 spellings rejected, list in the technique log) | high (re-asked every backfill day; never batch the raw ones) |\n| 74 | Config decoder routine as answer (algorithm, key, function name, loop shape) | gap (D17 prompt \"recover the reversible decoder\", unasked) | function xrefing the stored blob; `xor byte [..], imm8` / `xor al, 0x73` loops; Ada `pkg__decode_config` | [I] capstone over the function referencing the blob VA; `rizin -q -c 'aaa; axt @ <blob va>' f` | med (theme may be backfilled on d17 later) |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n```\nSTEP 1  file -b F ; xxd -l 64 F            -> container + arch + stripped/static/PIE in one line\n  7f454c46 ELF: byte4 1=ELF32 2=ELF64; byte5 1=LE 2=BE (BE => read e_machine/HCFG ints big-endian)\n  4d5a MZ->PE: Machine 0x14c i386 | 0x8664 x86-64 | 0xaa64 AArch64 | 0x1c0/0x1c4 ARM; \"Mono/.Net\" => pe_cli\n  cffaedfe/cefaedfe Mach-O thin; cafebabe + small u32 nfat => Mach-O FAT (NOT a Java class) ; format word presumed `macho`\n  504b0304 zip/jar/apk (keep nested jars whole) ; 1b4c7561 Lua ; 1b4c4a LuaJIT ; FOR1..BEAM Erlang ; 4243c0de LLVM bitcode\n  0061736d \\0asm WASM (D16): format `wasm`, architecture `wasm32` (GM-confirmed); lib.binary.wasm_layout -> sections, memories,\n    data_segments (file_offset + mem_offset); wasm-objdump -x F ; HCFG RAW in data seg 0 -> raw scan finds it (crc-gate)\n  ':10' text lines => Intel HEX ; 'S0'/'S1' => S-record ; no magic + ARM vector table => raw firmware (rizin -m base)\nSTEP 2  rz-bin -I F   (or readelf -hlSW F)  -> lang, machine, bits, endian, static, stripped, pic, relro, nx, canary\n  e_machine: 3 x86 | 62 x86-64 | 40 ARM | 183 AArch64 | 8 MIPS | 20 PPC | 21 PPC64 | 243 RISC-V | 2/43 SPARC\n  labels: GM-confirmed x86-64/x86/AArch64/ARM (ELF), i386/x86-64 (PE); others = readelf spelling first, then EM_ name minus\n  prefix; kind:integer => decimal e_machine. Dispatch on answer_format.kind, never on field name.\n  no .symtab => stripped (answer [] / none / false); no INTERP => static; ET_DYN+INTERP => PIE; ET_REL => object file\n  UPX0/UPX1 sections or \"UPX!\" or entropy>7.2 => PACKED: upx -t F; cp F /tmp/x; upx -d /tmp/x (fix zeroed UPX! first)\nSTEP 3  strings -a -n6 F | grep -m8 -E 'GCC:|clang|rustc|go1\\.|GHC |OCaml|caml_|FPC |Crystal|zig|GNAT Version|gfortran|DMD|Nim|\n        swift|_kDart|kfun:|__svm|MEI|nuitka|AU3!|Borland|MSVBVM|libcob|UPX|HCFG|SENGR'   -> toolchain + blob form\n  toolchain -> tool: Go GoReSym -t -d -p | Rust rustfilt | .NET ilspycmd | jar javap -v -p / jadx | Swift swift-demangle\n  Nim nim-demangle | PyInstaller pyinstxtractor+pycdc | AutoIt autoit-ripper | anything else: rizin -q -c 'aaa;afl' /\n  analyzeHeadless (lib.binary.ghidra_decompile) | foreign arch: rizin -a <arch> / llvm-objdump-18 / Ghidra (no exec, qemu absent)\nHCFG (every new member since D2)\n  python: from lib.binary import hcfg_find, hcfg_scan; hcfg_find(open(F,'rb').read())  -> config, offset, encoding, key, crc_ok\n  raw magic 'HCFG' | b64 'SENGR' | hex '48434647' | rot13 'FRATE' | b64-zlib 'eJ' | b64-gzip 'H4sI' -> covered by hcfg_scan\n  accept only crc32(plain)==header crc AND JSON parses; keep scanning past decoys (D9 had two raw-magic decoys)\n  NOT FOUND => blob is hidden: (1) packed? unpack; (2) AES S-box 637c777b / TEA 9e3779b9 / 'expand 32-byte k' => find key+IV\n  near the call, decrypt with pycryptodome; (3) runs of mov [rbp-x], imm => stack-built: collect imms with capstone or\n  emulate the builder with unicorn; (4) PE .rsrc / .NET resource / jar non-class entry / overlay past last section;\n  (5) .init_array / TLS callback decoder => emulate it. Offsets: raw=the H, base64=the S (GM-confirmed); else first stored byte.\nFIELDS: format = container only (elf/pe/macho?/jar; .NET pe_cli) | machine/architecture = container machine word |\n  qualifier ids dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field> -> member whose file name has <tag> (D15 stripped/symbolized, D16 compact/direct;\n  match the LONGEST member-name token, a tag may contain `_`) ; sha256_K = zip archive order | config_* verbatim from HCFG JSON |\n  has_<x>_section = literal section name | hex fields lowercase 0x | never chase the prompt's theme: answer only asked ids.\n  D17 Ada ELF (GNAT 14.2): plain ELF, HCFG RAW in .rodata -> carried-over solver answers it unchanged.\nBACKFILL ids on OLD groups (D8, D17): an unknown field on dNN = that day's own facts. Seen: marker (.huntress string),\n  recover_code (decimal imm), mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol (bare _ZNK.../_ZTI...; PE .text$/.rdata$), has_go_runtime,\n  has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime (enum true/false), methods (Main-Class method_info names incl <init>, JSON),\n  access_flags (decimal, 49), method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>). Derive from bytes, POST all derivable ones together.\nhcfg_storage: base64 literal -> `base64` (GM). RAW -> unknown word: send ALONE, cap ~10 probes, then HELP; never batch it.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"backfill-language-identity-facts\", \"concept\": \"Per-language identity + theme facts for the D8-D17 groups (the next backfill): has_<lang>_runtime / has_<lang>_mangled_symbol / class, protocol, selector, proc, template names\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 re-asked D1-D7's single-solve facts on their old groups (marker, recover_code, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_coroutine_runtime). Build ONE generic facts table so the D8-D17 analogues answer without code: has_swift_runtime (swift5_* sections / `$s` symbols), has_nim_runtime (NimMain), has_zig_runtime (.comment zig / `std.` panic strings), has_d_runtime (`_D4core`/`_D2rt`), has_fpc_runtime (FPC banner / `.fpcdata`), has_crystal_runtime (`Crystal:H`/`*crystal*`), has_objc_runtime (`__objc_*` sections, objc_msg_lookup), has_gnat_runtime (`GNAT Version`, `__gnat_`), has_wasm_*; plus name lists: ObjC classes/selectors (`._OBJC_CLASS_`, `objc_sel_name_`), Swift type/protocol names (demangled `$s` nominal types), Nim procs (`<proc>__<mod>_u<N>`), D functions (`_D<len>`), Ada subprograms (`pkg__sub`), mangled forms kept (GM wants MANGLED). Fixtures: the cached real members from day08-day17 single_solve/work/extracted (bytes on disk) + expected values in a table; every field returns `none`/`false` on absence, never raises.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-classfile-facts\", \"concept\": \"Full JVM ClassFile facts for jar groups (d06/d07): versions, constant-pool count, this/super/interfaces, fields, methods+descriptors, attributes, Kotlin metadata\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 asked methods (names, table order, incl <init>), access_flags (decimal 49) and method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>) of the Main-Class. Next backfill may ask major_version/minor_version, constant_pool_count, super_class, interfaces, field names/count, method descriptors, SourceFile attribute, main_class (Manifest), class_count/entry_count, Kotlin `@Metadata` d1/d2, invokeSuspend label states. Implement a stdlib ClassFile parser in lib (javap -v -p parity tests on fixture jars built with javac/kotlinc-free hand-made classes); JSON compact, table order, decimal ints.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-metadata-facts\", \"concept\": \".NET metadata facts for the d03 group: assembly name/version, MVID, TypeDef/MethodDef names, FieldRVA, TargetFramework, entry point token\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"d03 is the only old group whose day-facts were not re-asked on D17 (it got hcfg_version/xor_key_hex only); a later backfill likely asks typedef/method names, method_count, assembly_name, assembly_version, target_framework (runtimeconfig tfm), entry_point token hex, has_field_rva. Use dnfile (installed) + ilspycmd parity on a dotnet-built fixture dll; JSON lists in table order, `<Module>` and `<PrivateImplementationDetails>` kept as named.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"decoder-routine-locator\", \"concept\": \"Locate and characterise the config DECODER in the binary: function name, algorithm (xor/add/rol/rc4...), key/immediate, loop length, references to the stored blob\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 prompt: 'Recover the reversible decoder' (unasked, but a later backfill may ask decoder facts on d17 or any HCFG group). From the validated HcfgHit: compute blob VA, find code xrefs (RIP-relative lea/mov to VA in .text via capstone, or rizin `axt`), report the containing FUNC symbol (Ada `pkg__decode_config`, Nim/D/Crystal mangled kept), the xor immediate(s) inside the loop and whether it equals header key; return algorithm token `xor` speculative. Fixtures: gcc -O0/-O2 C decoders (xor, add, rol, rolling) with symbols and stripped.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"native-imports-exports-facts\", \"concept\": \"imports / NEEDED / interpreter / exports lists for ELF, PE, Mach-O\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Generic facts: ELF `needed` (DT_NEEDED order), `imports` (UND .dynsym names, table order, version suffix stripped), `interpreter` (.interp without NUL), `exports` (defined dynsyms); PE import dll list + functions (`dll!func`?), exports, imphash; Mach-O LC_LOAD_DYLIB. JSON compact like symbols. D15 symbolized had getenv/strcmp/printf, unasked. D17 backfill pattern (old days re-asked as per-group facts) makes imports/NEEDED lists a likely next field on any native group.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"provenance-facts-extractor\", \"concept\": \"Build provenance fields: GNU build-id, .comment compiler banner, DWARF producer/language/comp_dir, PE TimeDateStamp/PDB path/Rich, Go/Rust toolchain version\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Implement in the facts dict so a new id answers without code: build_id = lowercase hex of NT_GNU_BUILD_ID desc (no 0x), compiler = first `.comment` string, dwarf_producer via pyelftools, pdb_path from RSDS, timestamp as int and ISO. Fixtures from the existing TARGETS.json builds (gcc -g, -Wl,--build-id). Spellings unknown -> submit alone. D17 member had DWARF (Ada, producer `GNU Ada 14.2.0`): dwarf_language/producer is a plausible backfill id for d05/d11/d17.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"hcfg-storage-raw-label\", \"concept\": \"GM word for a RAW-stored HCFG in `hcfg_storage` (d12 FPC .data, d14 ObjC .hcfg)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D17: `base64` confirmed for SENGR literals; ~117 raw spellings rejected (raw, plain, bytes, binary, blob, xor, section, data, .data, .hcfg, rodata, struct, literal, inline, embedded, none, base64 and combos -- full list in the technique log). Untried: hex, encoded, xor_encoded, obfuscated, magic, header, framed, typed_const, array_of_byte, c_array, uint8_array, objc_section, fpc_data. When re-asked: submit raw ids ALONE after everything else banked, cap ~10 probes, then HELP; ask the organizers if a hint channel exists. Never let it hold the other ids.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"language-detector\", \"concept\": \"lib.binary.language_of(data) -> source language/toolchain token with evidence, for all 17 seen languages + next candidates\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A `language`/`compiler`/`toolchain` id on any group would need consistent tokens: c, cpp, csharp/dotnet, go, rust, java, kotlin, swift, nim, zig, d, pascal/fpc, crystal, objc, wat/wasm, ada; candidates haskell, ocaml, fortran, cobol, odin, v, dart, julia, kotlin-native, python(pyinstaller/nuitka). Cue table = atlas STEP 3 regex + section/symbol markers; verify on every cached dNN member (expected = the day's language), log ambiguity rather than guess.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"emulate-return-value\", \"concept\": \"Recover a function's return value by emulation when it is not a `mov eax, imm; ret` leaf (obfuscated/computed/OLLVM recover_code)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"recover_code was re-asked D17; a mutated variant may compute the constant (xor of two imms, lookup table, flattened switch). unicorn x86-64 (installed): map the ELF PT_LOADs, set rsp to a scratch stack, run from the FUNC symbol until ret with an instruction cap, read eax; refuse on syscalls/calls into libc. Fixtures: gcc -O0/-O2 builds with arithmetic-constant and table-lookup returns; AArch64 via unicorn ARM64 for the cross-arch case.\"},","numLines":168,"startLine":1,"totalLines":199,"truncatedByTokenCap":true}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NmjwkJFqKG5Pe7CDw9VoHs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
