{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NDZCxcZ71SZxppcTFMFR1K","type":"tool_result","content":"169\t  {\"id\": \"api-hashing-resolver\", \"concept\": \"Imports resolved by hash (ROR13, djb2, FNV-1a, CRC32, murmur) -> resolved API list / hash algorithm fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Natural 'encoded' sequel to D17 for a decoder-themed day. Precompute hash tables for libc/kernel32/ntdll export names under the common algorithms; scan .rodata/.text immediates (capstone `cmp`/`mov` imm32) and report matches in code order, algorithm token, seed. Fixtures: small C ELF/MinGW PE resolving getenv/printf by djb2 and ror13.\"},\n170\t  {\"id\": \"per-string-encryption\", \"concept\": \"Every string (not just HCFG) encrypted individually with a shared decoder (xor/add per string, stack strings) -> decoded string lists as fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Escalation of the D17 'encoded configuration' theme: config fields stored as separate xor'd strings instead of one HCFG blob. Use floss (installed in .venv) + a capstone pass collecting (ptr,len,key) triples from decoder call sites; decode all, crc/regex-gate (domains, BRNN-, Global\\\\\\\\). Fixtures: C ELF with 5 xor-encrypted strings + stack strings, -O0/-O2.\"},\n171\t  {\"id\": \"build-pair-router\", \"concept\": \"Same-source build PAIRS beyond stripped/symbolized and compact/direct (static/dynamic, O0/O2/Os, pie/nopie, debug/release, packed/unpacked, plain/obfuscated)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D15 and D16 were both 'one source, two builds' with `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` ids. Fixtures: gcc -O0 vs -O2, -static vs dynamic, -pie vs -no-pie, -g vs stripped, upx'd vs plain, each with a `.hcfg` section and file-name tags. Target: router matches the LONGEST tag token of exactly one member name; structural fallback per tag family (no INTERP = static, ET_DYN+INTERP = pie, UPX! = packed, .debug_info = debug, smaller code = compact/optimized); per-member fields that DIFFER inside a pair (elf_type, entry_point, has_symtab, section_names, imports) answered from that member; sha256_K from zip central-directory order.\"},\n172\t  {\"id\": \"cross-arch-pair\", \"concept\": \"Same source built for x86-64 + AArch64 (+ RISC-V/ARM .o) as a pair, arch-named qualifiers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15 links, clang-18 --target=riscv64/armv7 -c gives ET_REL. Name tags like `-x86_64.elf`/`-aarch64.elf`/`-arm64` put an UNDERSCORE inside the qualifier (`d17_analysis_x86_64_machine`): the router must try multi-token tags before splitting at the first `_`. Expected labels from multiarch-machine-labels (x86-64, AArch64, RISC-V, ARM; kind:integer 62/183/243/40); HCFG ints stay LE on these arches.\"},\n173\t  {\"id\": \"wasm-inventory-fields\", \"concept\": \"WASM 'doors' as answer fields: imports, exports, memory min/max/shared/memory64, table + elem (call_indirect targets), start, globals, data segment count/offsets, custom sections\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The D16 prompt named imports/memory/indirect calls but asked none; carry-over backfill may add them. Build fixtures with wat2wasm (installed): imports from env/wasi_snapshot_preview1 (func/memory/table/global), funcref table + active elem, call_indirect, start, mutable globals, passive segment, name + producers custom sections. Extend lib.binary.wasm_layout with imports [{module,name,kind}], exports [{name,kind,index}], tables, elems, start, globals, custom_names; candidate spellings: JSON list of `module.name` in section order, counts as integers, memory_min in pages, has_table true/false, hcfg_offset = file offset of the `H` (record mem_offset too).\"},\n174\t  {\"id\": \"ebpf-object\", \"concept\": \"eBPF ELF object (e_machine 247) with HCFG in .rodata / a map section\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"clang-18 -target bpf -O2 -c fixture with SEC(\\\"xdp\\\"), a `license` section, `.maps`, and an HCFG `.hcfg`/`.rodata` blob. Targets: format `elf`, elf_type ET_REL, machine readelf spelling `Linux BPF` (EM_BPF; integer 247), entry_point 0x0, has_hcfg_section; program section names as a possible `programs` field. Plausible next 'sandboxed code' after WASM.\"},\n175\t  {\"id\": \"sstrip-corrupt-headers\", \"concept\": \"ELF without section headers (sstrip, e_shnum=0) or with bogus e_shoff/e_shstrndx/fake section names\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: gcc build then python-zero e_shoff/e_shnum/e_shstrndx; another with garbage e_shstrndx; another with a section renamed to `.hcfg` that does not hold the blob. Targets: parser never crashes (pyelftools wrapped, header fields from raw struct), section_names `[]`, has_symtab false, has_hcfg_section false unless the literal name exists, HCFG via raw scan; entry_point/machine still from the ELF header.\"},\n176\t  {\"id\": \"qemu-user-static\", \"concept\": \"Run/observe foreign-arch ELF decoders (ARM/AArch64/MIPS/PPC/RISC-V)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install qemu-user-static binfmt-support (only qemu-system-* are installed now). Use only inside the bwrap sandbox, never on the host; static analysis remains the default.\"},\n177\t  {\"id\": \"diec\", \"concept\": \"Compiler/packer/language fingerprint for unknown toolchains\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release horsicq/DIE-engine (die_lin64_portable tar) -> `diec -j F`. Complements `rz-bin -I` lang= and the STEP 3 strings regex when a new language lands.\"},\n178\t  {\"id\": \"checksec-fields\", \"concept\": \"PIE/RELRO/NX/canary/static as answer fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"`rz-bin -I` already prints pic/relro/nx/canary/static/stripped. GM spelling unknown: relro full/partial/none, booleans true/false like has_symtab. Add to playbook naming law before first sighting; no checksec install needed.\"},\n179\t  {\"id\": \"new-language-fingerprints\", \"concept\": \"Haskell, OCaml, Fortran, V, Odin, COBOL, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka (Ada seen D17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Cue strings are in the Recognition cues STEP 3 regex. All still answer format=elf/architecture=x86-64 per the D8-D15 law; risk is only where the HCFG literal lives (compressed Dart snapshot, Nuitka constants blob, GHC closures) -> hcfg_scan then Ghidra. Ada landed D17 as a plain ELF with RAW HCFG -- the law held. gfortran/gnat/ocaml/ghc are NOT installed for fixture builds (apt gfortran gnat ocaml-nox ghc if prebuilds are wanted).\"},\n180\t  {\"id\": \"wasm-hcfg-hidden\", \"concept\": \"WASM HCFG not a plain active data segment: custom section `hcfg`, passive segment + memory.init, split across segments, built by i32.store immediates, UTF-16 (AssemblyScript), memory64 module\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Natural Mastery/next-day twist of D16. Fixtures via wat2wasm: (a) custom section named hcfg (has_hcfg_section analogue -> `true`), (b) passive segment, (c) blob split over two active segments at adjacent mem offsets (reassemble linear memory image then hcfg_find), (d) code-built: run of `i32.const addr; i32.const imm; i32.store` -> collect imms in order (or a tiny stack interpreter over the function body), (e) memory64 limits flag 0x04 -> machine `wasm64` speculative. Never execute the module (no wasmtime).\"},\n181\t  {\"id\": \"bytecode-containers\", \"concept\": \"LLVM bitcode, Python .pyc, Lua luac, standalone .class/.dex as group members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: clang-18 -c -emit-llvm (BC C0 DE + wrapper), python -m py_compile (3.x magic), luac (installed), javac single class. Record magic -> candidate format labels (`llvm_bitcode`/`bitcode`, `pyc`, `luac`/`lua`, `class`, `dex`) and architecture (`none`?); HCFG as a string constant (raw or base64) -> hcfg_scan; submit any new label alone.\"},\n182\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-singlefile-aot\", \"concept\": \".NET single-file bundle, ReadyToRun and NativeAOT builds\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"dotnet installed: `dotnet publish -p:PublishSingleFile=true` (apphost + bundle manifest, `.net core bundle` signature hash), `-p:PublishReadyToRun=true` (R2R header in CLI dll), `-p:PublishAot=true` (native ELF, no BSJB). Targets: format label shift (pe_cli vs elf), HCFG location inside the bundle (embedded dll offset) -> hcfg_scan on the bundle bytes.\"},\n183\t  {\"id\": \"de4dot\", \"concept\": \"ConfuserEx / .NET string encryption\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github de4dot-cex (ViRb3) release; needs apt mono-runtime. `de4dot F -o clean.dll` then ilspycmd.\"},\n184\t  {\"id\": \"erlang-lua-decompilers\", \"concept\": \"BEAM, Lua, LuaJIT bytecode\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"luac (lua5.4) is now installed. Still missing: apt erlang-base (beam_lib/beam_disasm), unluac jar (sourceforge), luajit-decompiler-v2 (github marsinator358) -- only if a bytecode container appears.\"},\n185\t  {\"id\": \"binutils-multiarch\", \"concept\": \"objdump/readelf for MIPS/PPC/SPARC/RISC-V\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install binutils-multiarch; rizin, llvm-objdump-18 and Ghidra already cover disassembly, so this is a convenience only.\"},\n186\t  {\"id\": \"ihex-srec-firmware\", \"concept\": \"Intel HEX / S-record / raw firmware members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"objcopy -I ihex|srec -O binary already converts (srecord not needed). For raw blobs: rizin -a arm -b 16 -m <base>; format label unknown (`ihex`/`srec`/`raw`?) -> submit alone.\"},\n187\t  {\"id\": \"upx-packed-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"UPX-packed ELF/PE (plain and with scrubbed UPX! magic / renamed sections)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture: `upx -9` a C ELF + MinGW PE carrying an HCFG `.hcfg` section; variant with `UPX!` zeroed and UPX0/1 renamed. Target: solver detects (packer_info), restores magic, `upx -d` on a copy, then hcfg_find + header fields of the UNPACKED image; record which bytes (packed vs unpacked) sha256/format/has_hcfg_section are answered from. upx 4.2.4 installed.\"},\n188\t  {\"id\": \"aes-tea-chacha-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"HCFG encrypted with AES-128/256 (ECB/CBC/CTR), XTEA, ChaCha20\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture style of TARGETS.json: key/IV as adjacent 16/32-byte raw or printable strings, or derived (sha256 of campaign-like string). Extractor: locate cipher by constants (S-box 637c777b, 0x9e3779b9, 'expand 32-byte k'), try candidate keys within +-4 KB, accept when plaintext starts 'HCFG' and crc-gates. pycryptodome installed.\"},\n189\t  {\"id\": \"stack-built-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"HCFG assembled at runtime from mov-immediate stores / per-char pushes\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture: gcc -O0/-O2 C that writes the blob via volatile stack stores (x86-64 and AArch64). Extractor: capstone imm collection per function in store order, fallback unicorn emulation of the builder (no syscalls), then hcfg_find on the buffer. Offset convention unknown: record the first mov instruction's file offset as a speculative guess.\"},\n190\t  {\"id\": \"multiarch-machine-labels\", \"concept\": \"ELF/PE/Mach-O machine words for i386, ARM, AArch64, MIPS(el), PPC/PPC64, RISC-V, SPARC + big-endian HCFG ints\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib/knowledge.py ELF_MACHINE has only 4 entries. Fixtures: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc (linkable) and clang-18 --target=<arch> -c (ET_REL .o; no lld installed) each with a `.hcfg` section, LE and BE. Expected labels = readelf spelling (x86, ARM, AArch64, MIPS R3000, PowerPC, PowerPC64, RISC-V, Sparc v9) with decimal e_machine for kind:integer; check hcfg_scan handles BE u16/u32 header fields.\"},\n191\t  {\"id\": \"macho-hcfg-section\", \"concept\": \"Mach-O thin + fat universal binary with HCFG in a `__DATA,__hcfg` section\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"clang-18 --target=x86_64-apple-macos -c and arm64-apple-macos -c produce MH_OBJECT files (no ld64); hand-pack a FAT header with python for the universal case. Targets: format label (`macho` presumed), machine from cputype (0x01000007 -> x86-64, 0x0100000c -> AArch64), has_hcfg_section on segment,section names, fat-vs-Java cafebabe disambiguation, lib.binary.macho_facts over both slices.\"},\n192\t  {\"id\": \"resource-overlay-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"HCFG in PE RT_RCDATA, .NET manifest resource, jar non-class entry, or file overlay\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: MinGW-free path = patch a resource dir with pefile into a small PE; dnfile resource in a dotnet-built dll; jar with config.bin; ELF/PE with blob appended past the last section. Confirm hcfg_scan finds each and record offset convention (resource data start vs magic) plus a speculative has_overlay/overlay_offset.\"},\n193\t  {\"id\": \"rolling-xor-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"Index-dependent xor (key+i, key^prev, xor with len/crc)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend the bytemap/mxor fixture family: known-plaintext 'HCFG' recovers the start key and step; brute 256 x {add,sub,xor-prev} modes, crc-gate. Not covered by current single-byte or repeating-key xor.\"},\n194\t  {\"id\": \"init-time-decoder\", \"concept\": \"Config decoded in .init_array constructor / TLS callback / DllMain\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture with __attribute__((constructor)) decoding a stored blob; extractor finds .init_array targets and emulates them with unicorn (stdlib-free). Low until a day theme hints at runtime behaviour.\"},\n195\t  {\"id\": \"shared-object-relocatable\", \"concept\": \"ET_DYN .so / ET_REL .o / DLL members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"gcc -shared and gcc -c fixtures with .hcfg; expected elf_type ET_DYN/ET_REL, entry_point 0x0 for .o, exported-symbol config. PE DLL via objdump -p export table.\"},\n196\t  {\"id\": \"exotic-codecs\", \"concept\": \"base58/base62/base91/z85 and lz4/zstd/brotli HCFG\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"tools/pybase62 + tools/pybase91 + python lz4 exist; pip install zstandard brotli into the venv. Add hcfg_fixtures entries with speculative offset = first stored byte.\"}\n197\t]\n198\t```\n199\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41c40dd5-eb72-4691-b80c-2f2f7cef8026","uuid":"453bb1fa-c571-43b3-8c46-9682e2c72706","timestamp":"2026-10-17T17:10:34.032Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md","content":"  {\"id\": \"api-hashing-resolver\", \"concept\": \"Imports resolved by hash (ROR13, djb2, FNV-1a, CRC32, murmur) -> resolved API list / hash algorithm fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Natural 'encoded' sequel to D17 for a decoder-themed day. Precompute hash tables for libc/kernel32/ntdll export names under the common algorithms; scan .rodata/.text immediates (capstone `cmp`/`mov` imm32) and report matches in code order, algorithm token, seed. Fixtures: small C ELF/MinGW PE resolving getenv/printf by djb2 and ror13.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"per-string-encryption\", \"concept\": \"Every string (not just HCFG) encrypted individually with a shared decoder (xor/add per string, stack strings) -> decoded string lists as fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Escalation of the D17 'encoded configuration' theme: config fields stored as separate xor'd strings instead of one HCFG blob. Use floss (installed in .venv) + a capstone pass collecting (ptr,len,key) triples from decoder call sites; decode all, crc/regex-gate (domains, BRNN-, Global\\\\\\\\). Fixtures: C ELF with 5 xor-encrypted strings + stack strings, -O0/-O2.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"build-pair-router\", \"concept\": \"Same-source build PAIRS beyond stripped/symbolized and compact/direct (static/dynamic, O0/O2/Os, pie/nopie, debug/release, packed/unpacked, plain/obfuscated)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D15 and D16 were both 'one source, two builds' with `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` ids. Fixtures: gcc -O0 vs -O2, -static vs dynamic, -pie vs -no-pie, -g vs stripped, upx'd vs plain, each with a `.hcfg` section and file-name tags. Target: router matches the LONGEST tag token of exactly one member name; structural fallback per tag family (no INTERP = static, ET_DYN+INTERP = pie, UPX! = packed, .debug_info = debug, smaller code = compact/optimized); per-member fields that DIFFER inside a pair (elf_type, entry_point, has_symtab, section_names, imports) answered from that member; sha256_K from zip central-directory order.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cross-arch-pair\", \"concept\": \"Same source built for x86-64 + AArch64 (+ RISC-V/ARM .o) as a pair, arch-named qualifiers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15 links, clang-18 --target=riscv64/armv7 -c gives ET_REL. Name tags like `-x86_64.elf`/`-aarch64.elf`/`-arm64` put an UNDERSCORE inside the qualifier (`d17_analysis_x86_64_machine`): the router must try multi-token tags before splitting at the first `_`. Expected labels from multiarch-machine-labels (x86-64, AArch64, RISC-V, ARM; kind:integer 62/183/243/40); HCFG ints stay LE on these arches.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"wasm-inventory-fields\", \"concept\": \"WASM 'doors' as answer fields: imports, exports, memory min/max/shared/memory64, table + elem (call_indirect targets), start, globals, data segment count/offsets, custom sections\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The D16 prompt named imports/memory/indirect calls but asked none; carry-over backfill may add them. Build fixtures with wat2wasm (installed): imports from env/wasi_snapshot_preview1 (func/memory/table/global), funcref table + active elem, call_indirect, start, mutable globals, passive segment, name + producers custom sections. Extend lib.binary.wasm_layout with imports [{module,name,kind}], exports [{name,kind,index}], tables, elems, start, globals, custom_names; candidate spellings: JSON list of `module.name` in section order, counts as integers, memory_min in pages, has_table true/false, hcfg_offset = file offset of the `H` (record mem_offset too).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ebpf-object\", \"concept\": \"eBPF ELF object (e_machine 247) with HCFG in .rodata / a map section\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"clang-18 -target bpf -O2 -c fixture with SEC(\\\"xdp\\\"), a `license` section, `.maps`, and an HCFG `.hcfg`/`.rodata` blob. Targets: format `elf`, elf_type ET_REL, machine readelf spelling `Linux BPF` (EM_BPF; integer 247), entry_point 0x0, has_hcfg_section; program section names as a possible `programs` field. Plausible next 'sandboxed code' after WASM.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sstrip-corrupt-headers\", \"concept\": \"ELF without section headers (sstrip, e_shnum=0) or with bogus e_shoff/e_shstrndx/fake section names\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: gcc build then python-zero e_shoff/e_shnum/e_shstrndx; another with garbage e_shstrndx; another with a section renamed to `.hcfg` that does not hold the blob. Targets: parser never crashes (pyelftools wrapped, header fields from raw struct), section_names `[]`, has_symtab false, has_hcfg_section false unless the literal name exists, HCFG via raw scan; entry_point/machine still from the ELF header.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"qemu-user-static\", \"concept\": \"Run/observe foreign-arch ELF decoders (ARM/AArch64/MIPS/PPC/RISC-V)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install qemu-user-static binfmt-support (only qemu-system-* are installed now). Use only inside the bwrap sandbox, never on the host; static analysis remains the default.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"diec\", \"concept\": \"Compiler/packer/language fingerprint for unknown toolchains\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release horsicq/DIE-engine (die_lin64_portable tar) -> `diec -j F`. Complements `rz-bin -I` lang= and the STEP 3 strings regex when a new language lands.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"checksec-fields\", \"concept\": \"PIE/RELRO/NX/canary/static as answer fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"`rz-bin -I` already prints pic/relro/nx/canary/static/stripped. GM spelling unknown: relro full/partial/none, booleans true/false like has_symtab. Add to playbook naming law before first sighting; no checksec install needed.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-language-fingerprints\", \"concept\": \"Haskell, OCaml, Fortran, V, Odin, COBOL, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka (Ada seen D17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Cue strings are in the Recognition cues STEP 3 regex. All still answer format=elf/architecture=x86-64 per the D8-D15 law; risk is only where the HCFG literal lives (compressed Dart snapshot, Nuitka constants blob, GHC closures) -> hcfg_scan then Ghidra. Ada landed D17 as a plain ELF with RAW HCFG -- the law held. gfortran/gnat/ocaml/ghc are NOT installed for fixture builds (apt gfortran gnat ocaml-nox ghc if prebuilds are wanted).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"wasm-hcfg-hidden\", \"concept\": \"WASM HCFG not a plain active data segment: custom section `hcfg`, passive segment + memory.init, split across segments, built by i32.store immediates, UTF-16 (AssemblyScript), memory64 module\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Natural Mastery/next-day twist of D16. Fixtures via wat2wasm: (a) custom section named hcfg (has_hcfg_section analogue -> `true`), (b) passive segment, (c) blob split over two active segments at adjacent mem offsets (reassemble linear memory image then hcfg_find), (d) code-built: run of `i32.const addr; i32.const imm; i32.store` -> collect imms in order (or a tiny stack interpreter over the function body), (e) memory64 limits flag 0x04 -> machine `wasm64` speculative. Never execute the module (no wasmtime).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bytecode-containers\", \"concept\": \"LLVM bitcode, Python .pyc, Lua luac, standalone .class/.dex as group members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: clang-18 -c -emit-llvm (BC C0 DE + wrapper), python -m py_compile (3.x magic), luac (installed), javac single class. Record magic -> candidate format labels (`llvm_bitcode`/`bitcode`, `pyc`, `luac`/`lua`, `class`, `dex`) and architecture (`none`?); HCFG as a string constant (raw or base64) -> hcfg_scan; submit any new label alone.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-singlefile-aot\", \"concept\": \".NET single-file bundle, ReadyToRun and NativeAOT builds\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"dotnet installed: `dotnet publish -p:PublishSingleFile=true` (apphost + bundle manifest, `.net core bundle` signature hash), `-p:PublishReadyToRun=true` (R2R header in CLI dll), `-p:PublishAot=true` (native ELF, no BSJB). Targets: format label shift (pe_cli vs elf), HCFG location inside the bundle (embedded dll offset) -> hcfg_scan on the bundle bytes.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"de4dot\", \"concept\": \"ConfuserEx / .NET string encryption\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github de4dot-cex (ViRb3) release; needs apt mono-runtime. `de4dot F -o clean.dll` then ilspycmd.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"erlang-lua-decompilers\", \"concept\": \"BEAM, Lua, LuaJIT bytecode\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"luac (lua5.4) is now installed. Still missing: apt erlang-base (beam_lib/beam_disasm), unluac jar (sourceforge), luajit-decompiler-v2 (github marsinator358) -- only if a bytecode container appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"binutils-multiarch\", \"concept\": \"objdump/readelf for MIPS/PPC/SPARC/RISC-V\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install binutils-multiarch; rizin, llvm-objdump-18 and Ghidra already cover disassembly, so this is a convenience only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ihex-srec-firmware\", \"concept\": \"Intel HEX / S-record / raw firmware members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"objcopy -I ihex|srec -O binary already converts (srecord not needed). For raw blobs: rizin -a arm -b 16 -m <base>; format label unknown (`ihex`/`srec`/`raw`?) -> submit alone.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"upx-packed-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"UPX-packed ELF/PE (plain and with scrubbed UPX! magic / renamed sections)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture: `upx -9` a C ELF + MinGW PE carrying an HCFG `.hcfg` section; variant with `UPX!` zeroed and UPX0/1 renamed. Target: solver detects (packer_info), restores magic, `upx -d` on a copy, then hcfg_find + header fields of the UNPACKED image; record which bytes (packed vs unpacked) sha256/format/has_hcfg_section are answered from. upx 4.2.4 installed.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"aes-tea-chacha-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"HCFG encrypted with AES-128/256 (ECB/CBC/CTR), XTEA, ChaCha20\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture style of TARGETS.json: key/IV as adjacent 16/32-byte raw or printable strings, or derived (sha256 of campaign-like string). Extractor: locate cipher by constants (S-box 637c777b, 0x9e3779b9, 'expand 32-byte k'), try candidate keys within +-4 KB, accept when plaintext starts 'HCFG' and crc-gates. pycryptodome installed.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stack-built-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"HCFG assembled at runtime from mov-immediate stores / per-char pushes\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture: gcc -O0/-O2 C that writes the blob via volatile stack stores (x86-64 and AArch64). Extractor: capstone imm collection per function in store order, fallback unicorn emulation of the builder (no syscalls), then hcfg_find on the buffer. Offset convention unknown: record the first mov instruction's file offset as a speculative guess.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"multiarch-machine-labels\", \"concept\": \"ELF/PE/Mach-O machine words for i386, ARM, AArch64, MIPS(el), PPC/PPC64, RISC-V, SPARC + big-endian HCFG ints\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib/knowledge.py ELF_MACHINE has only 4 entries. Fixtures: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc (linkable) and clang-18 --target=<arch> -c (ET_REL .o; no lld installed) each with a `.hcfg` section, LE and BE. Expected labels = readelf spelling (x86, ARM, AArch64, MIPS R3000, PowerPC, PowerPC64, RISC-V, Sparc v9) with decimal e_machine for kind:integer; check hcfg_scan handles BE u16/u32 header fields.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"macho-hcfg-section\", \"concept\": \"Mach-O thin + fat universal binary with HCFG in a `__DATA,__hcfg` section\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"clang-18 --target=x86_64-apple-macos -c and arm64-apple-macos -c produce MH_OBJECT files (no ld64); hand-pack a FAT header with python for the universal case. Targets: format label (`macho` presumed), machine from cputype (0x01000007 -> x86-64, 0x0100000c -> AArch64), has_hcfg_section on segment,section names, fat-vs-Java cafebabe disambiguation, lib.binary.macho_facts over both slices.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"resource-overlay-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"HCFG in PE RT_RCDATA, .NET manifest resource, jar non-class entry, or file overlay\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: MinGW-free path = patch a resource dir with pefile into a small PE; dnfile resource in a dotnet-built dll; jar with config.bin; ELF/PE with blob appended past the last section. Confirm hcfg_scan finds each and record offset convention (resource data start vs magic) plus a speculative has_overlay/overlay_offset.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"rolling-xor-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"Index-dependent xor (key+i, key^prev, xor with len/crc)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend the bytemap/mxor fixture family: known-plaintext 'HCFG' recovers the start key and step; brute 256 x {add,sub,xor-prev} modes, crc-gate. Not covered by current single-byte or repeating-key xor.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"init-time-decoder\", \"concept\": \"Config decoded in .init_array constructor / TLS callback / DllMain\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture with __attribute__((constructor)) decoding a stored blob; extractor finds .init_array targets and emulates them with unicorn (stdlib-free). Low until a day theme hints at runtime behaviour.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"shared-object-relocatable\", \"concept\": \"ET_DYN .so / ET_REL .o / DLL members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"gcc -shared and gcc -c fixtures with .hcfg; expected elf_type ET_DYN/ET_REL, entry_point 0x0 for .o, exported-symbol config. PE DLL via objdump -p export table.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"exotic-codecs\", \"concept\": \"base58/base62/base91/z85 and lz4/zstd/brotli HCFG\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"tools/pybase62 + tools/pybase91 + python lz4 exist; pip install zstandard brotli into the venv. Add hcfg_fixtures entries with speculative offset = first stored byte.\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":31,"startLine":169,"totalLines":199}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NDZCxcZ71SZxppcTFMFR1K","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
