{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8BUJH75AhSSNzAncoBq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016F1B9D4xFG8RK8K9wDk6ew","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'E'\np='reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,(a[:60],s.count(a)); s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"\"\"- The analysis is easy (headers, symbols, one config blob). The hard part is the GM's exact label for `exact_text` fields\n  (format, machine, symbol, D17 `hcfg_storage`).\"\"\",\"\"\"- The analysis is easy (headers, symbols, one config blob). The hard part is the GM's exact label for `exact_text` fields\n  (format, machine, symbol, D17 `hcfg_storage`). **The organizers RE-ISSUE the contract mid-day** when a label is unguessable:\n  D17's `hcfg_storage` became `kind: enum` + `accepted_values` + an ordered rule list in the question text (and 20 other ids got\n  rule text that accepts equivalents). Re-pull the contract while stuck; never out-guess it.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"5 D15-D17; D17 contract 5 x 204\n  = 1020 ids); artifacts are named `delivery N: evidence.zip`. D17 TT/Mastery were never started (single stuck at 202/204).\"\"\",\"\"\"5 D15-D17; D17 contract 5 x 204\n  = 1020 ids); artifacts are named `delivery N: evidence.zip`. D17 timed windows: TT 5 s, Mastery 14 s end to end.\"\"\")\n# variant axes: hcfg_storage\ni=s.index(\"- **Storage-as-answer (`hcfg_storage`\"); j=s.index(\"- **Any other storage encoding\")\ns=s[:i]+\"\"\"- **Storage-as-answer (`hcfg_storage`, NEW D17, asked on d08/d09/d11/d12/d13/d14)** -- revised contract: `kind: enum`,\n  `accepted_values` [raw, base64, raw_const_array, raw_hcfg_section, wasm_data_segment], rules applied IN ORDER: `base64` if the\n  crc-valid HCFG appears only after decoding a printable base64 carrier (d08 Swift, d09 Nim, d11 D, d13 Crystal) ->\n  `raw_hcfg_section` if literal `HCFG` starts inside a section named exactly `.hcfg` (d14 ObjC; section headers suffice) ->\n  `wasm_data_segment` if inside a WASM data segment -> `raw_const_array` if inside any OTHER native data section (d12 FPC `.data`;\n  by the rule also Ada/Go/Rust `.rodata`) -> else `raw`. Rule: take the validated hit's encoding + `section containing its\n  file offset` (map offset -> section header; PE/Mach-O the same) and walk the list; jars = base64 (constant-pool literal).\n  Unknown future token: read the question's rule list first -- the enum is the answer space.\n\"\"\"+s[j:]\nrep(\"\"\"(D15 TT BR15-005; D16 TT == the single); a carry-over d01 can differ (D9 Mastery `mov eax, 8104`; D15-D16 Mastery set1 d01\n  STRIPPED -> symbols/disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`, and D17's re-asked `recover_code`/`marker` would then be `none`).\n  Pair by sha256, never index.\"\"\",\"\"\"(D15 TT BR15-005; D16 TT == the single); a carry-over d01 can differ (D9 Mastery `mov eax, 8104`; D15-D16 Mastery set1 d01\n  STRIPPED -> symbols/disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`). D17 CONFIRMED: TT d01 and all 5 Mastery d01s stripped ->\n  `recover_code` = `none` although `kind: integer` (the leaf heuristic's 8114/8106 were rejected). Pair by sha256, never index.\n- **Contract wording per fetch (D17)** -- the SAME id's question text/answer_format changed between the morning and the revised\n  contract (exact_text -> enum for hcfg_storage; section_names now \"leading \\\\\"\\\\\" optional\"; compression_methods codes OR names;\n  format/machine \"bitness-qualified labels accepted\"). Rule: the solver reads `answer_format` per id at run time\n  (`accepted_values` = closed answer set; assert the emitted token is in it); keep the GM-confirmed spelling when both pass.\"\"\")\n# cues table row\nrep(\"\"\"| Packed / high entropy / `UPX!` |\"\"\",\"\"\"| `answer_format.kind: enum` + `accepted_values`, question says \"Apply these mutually exclusive rules in order\" | The question IS the spec: implement the rules top-down over the parsed facts, emit one listed token (D17 hcfg_storage) |\n| Packed / high entropy / `UPX!` |\"\"\")\n# day entry\ni=s.index(\"**D17 \\\"Decoder Ring\\\"**\"); j=s.index(\"## GM answer conventions learned\")\ns=s[:i]+\"\"\"**D17 \"Decoder Ring\"** (slug `encoded-configuration-recovery`; 204 Qs; CORRECT at **T+4:03**; TT CORRECT 2nd try, Mastery\nCORRECT after 5 per-set fixes). Prompt: \"Recover the reversible decoder and read what it was hiding.\" New group = ONE Ada ELF\n(1.39 MB, GNAT 14.2.0, dynamic glibc, not stripped, DWARF); HCFG RAW in `.rodata` (ver 1, key 0x73) -- the usual 1-byte-xor\nHCFG, no new encoding, decoder never asked.\n- d17 group (12 ids) + 176 carry-over ids banked at **T+18 s** by the carried-over solver -- zero code for the new language.\n- Backfill #2 (32 new ids on old groups): 22 already covered by the generic facts dict; 10 needed code, all accepted in ONE POST\n  at T+2:40 (d01 marker/recover_code, d02 mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol, d04 has_go_runtime, d05 has_rust_mangled_symbol,\n  d06 methods/access_flags, d07 method_count/has_coroutine_runtime -- spellings in the conventions table).\n- `hcfg_storage`: `base64` (d08/d09/d11/d13) banked by T+4:13. The 2 raw ids (d12, d14) then burned **~10.9k single-id rejected\n  POSTs** (~117 by the worker + automated label grouptests, ~3.5 h) until the organizers re-issued the contract with an enum:\n  `raw_hcfg_section` (d14) / `raw_const_array` (d12) -> CORRECT within a minute of the revision being pulled.\n- TT: 1st submit wrong only on `d01_analysis_recover_code` -- TT d01 was STRIPPED and the D17 `recover_code` code fell back to the\n  leaf `mov eax, imm; ret` scan (8114); `none` -> CORRECT (TT phases: solve 1.0 s, total 5 s). Mastery: same bug on all 5 sets\n  (8106) -> `none` per set -> CORRECT (14 s total, solve 5.1 s). Time lost: the label tail; the d01 bug had been PREDICTED in the\n  Variant axes (D15-D16 Mastery d01 stripped) but the new field's code did not apply the family's absence rule.\n\n\"\"\"+s[j:]\n# conventions\ni=s.index(\"| hcfg_storage (exact_text, D17) |\"); j=s.index(\"\\n\",i)\ns=s[:i]+\"| hcfg_storage (enum, D17 revised contract) | `base64` (SENGR literal), `raw_hcfg_section` (in a `.hcfg` section), `raw_const_array` (other native data section, e.g. FPC `.data`), `wasm_data_segment`, `raw` (else) | every free-text spelling for raw-stored (raw, raw_data, section, .hcfg, bytes, blob, ... ~10.9k probes) -- the token set is closed |\"+s[j:]\nrep(\"| recover_code | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` → 8100); `none` if the function is absent | the renamed function's constant |\",\n    \"| recover_code (`kind: integer`) | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` → 8100); `none` if the symbol is absent (stripped d01, D17 TT+Mastery CONFIRMED) | the stripped/renamed leaf's constant (8114, 8106) |\")\nrep(\"| section_names (JSON) | pyelftools order INCLUDING the leading `\\\"\\\"` |\",\"| section_names (JSON) | pyelftools order INCLUDING the leading `\\\"\\\"` (D17 revised text: omitting it also accepted) |\")\nrep(\"| compression_methods (jar, json) | sorted distinct ZIP method ids, compact: `[0,8]` |\",\"| compression_methods (jar, json) | sorted distinct ZIP method ids, compact: `[0,8]` (D17 text: Stored/Deflate names, any order also accepted) |\")\n# pitfalls\nrep(\"\"\"- **A synthetic label with no derivable spelling** (D3 .NET format ~1.5 h; D17 raw `hcfg_storage`, ~117 POSTs, never found): stop\n  after ~10 single-id probes plus one `hctf labels` run, write HELP.md, and let the rest of the day proceed. Never put the\n  unknown id into a batch with other open ids.\"\"\",\"\"\"- **A synthetic label with no derivable spelling** (D3 .NET format ~1.5 h; D17 raw `hcfg_storage`, ~10.9k POSTs over 3.5 h,\n  NEVER guessed -- solved only by the organizers' contract revision to an enum): stop after ~10 single-id probes plus one `hctf\n  labels` run, write HELP.md, then RE-PULL THE CONTRACT periodically and diff each id's question/answer_format. Never put the\n  unknown id into a batch with other open ids; mass automated grouptests on an exact_text label are wasted POSTs.\n- **A re-asked field must inherit its family's absence rule** (D17 TT/Mastery): new `recover_code` code fell back to a leaf\n  heuristic on a stripped d01 although `disassembly` had learnt `[]` on D8. Absent symbol => `none`/`[]`/`false`, always.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\nwc -l reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md; sed -i '1s/.*/# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-17; updated after every day)/' reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4526,"cache_read_input_tokens":97447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4526},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41c40dd5-eb72-4691-b80c-2f2f7cef8026","uuid":"50d00f43-f0c9-4ff5-b4d6-f9d8f2f6ce6d","timestamp":"2026-10-17T17:11:57.832Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8BUHvWrUUFhV3dbQxX6","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016F1B9D4xFG8RK8K9wDk6ew":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'E'\np='reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,(a[:60],s.count(a)); s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"\"\"- The analysis is easy (headers, symbols, one config blob). The hard part is the GM's exact label for `exact_text` fields\n  (format, machine, symbol, D17 `hcfg_storage`).\"\"\",\"\"\"- The analysis is easy (headers, symbols, one config blob). The hard part is the GM's exact label for `exact_text` fields\n  (format, machine, symbol, D17 `hcfg_storage`). **The organizers RE-ISSUE the contract mid-day** whe