{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8BZmXbNTSvxnurjLUg1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WQ2DPFYkfTzUuuFha41rQZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n\")+len(\"## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n\"); j=s.index(\"```\",i)\nold=json.loads(s[i:j])\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\ndef built(g): \n    v=st.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+g['id'],{}); return v.get('ok') or v.get('attempts',0)>=2\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"hcfg-storage-classifier\",\"concept\":\"Generic `hcfg_storage` token for EVERY group/container per the D17 GM rule list (base64 / raw_hcfg_section / wasm_data_segment / raw_const_array / raw)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D17 asked it on d08/d09/d11-d14 only; the next backfill likely spreads it (as hcfg_offset spread) to d02 (ELF `.hcfg` or PE `.hcfg` COFF section), d03 (.NET FieldRVA blob inside PE `.text` -> by the rules `raw_const_array` only if the section is a data section, else `raw` -- record both as uncertain), d04 Go/d05 Rust/d17 Ada `.rodata` (raw_const_array), d06/d07 jars (base64 in a deflated constant pool -> `base64`), d10 `.hcfg` (raw_hcfg_section), d15 pair, d16 wasm (wasm_data_segment). Implement `lib.binary.hcfg_storage(data, hit)` = rules applied in order over (hit.encoding, container, section containing hit.offset with its flags: SHF_ALLOC && !SHF_EXECINSTR = data; PE IMAGE_SCN_CNT_INITIALIZED_DATA; Mach-O __DATA/__DATA_CONST/__TEXT,__const). Tests: every cached day02-day17 member on disk (GM-confirmed d08/d09/d11-d14 tokens as expected values) + synthetic `.hcfg`/.data/.rodata/.text/PE/wasm fixtures; return None (not a guess) when the hit lies in no section.\"},\n {\"id\":\"question-rule-extractor\",\"concept\":\"Read the contract's per-id rule text + `accepted_values` and enforce it pre-submit (organizer revisions turn labels into enums)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D17: the organizers re-issued the contract mid-day; hcfg_storage became kind enum with accepted_values and 'Apply these mutually exclusive rules in order: <token> when <cond>; ...; otherwise <token>'. Build a lane helper that (a) parses `(token, condition)` pairs out of such question text, (b) exposes `accepted_values` per id to the solver, (c) refuses to emit a token outside accepted_values (empty + log instead), (d) diffs two contract snapshots per id (question/answer_format changed) so a stuck worker sees the revision immediately. Tests: D17 single_solve morning vs revised contract.json (both on disk if cached; otherwise synthetic pair).\"},\n {\"id\":\"offset-section-mapper\",\"concept\":\"Map a file offset to its container location: ELF section + segment (name, flags, VA), PE section (name, RVA, VA), Mach-O segment,section, WASM data segment index + memory offset\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Underpins hcfg_storage and the likely next location ids (`hcfg_section`, `hcfg_va`/`hcfg_vaddr`, `hcfg_rva`, `hcfg_segment`, `hcfg_mem_offset`). `lib.binary.locate_offset(data, off)` -> {container, section, section_flags, segment_index, vaddr, rva, wasm_data_index, wasm_mem_offset}; pure struct parsing (no pyelftools exceptions on sstripped files: fall back to program headers). Expected spellings to try first: section name verbatim (`.rodata`), VA as lowercase `0x` hex like entry_point. Tests on cached day08-day17 members (D17 Ada blob at file 207432 in `.rodata`, D14 at 4000 in `.hcfg`, D12 at 82928 in `.data`) and the wasm fixtures.\"},\n {\"id\":\"elf-header-segment-facts\",\"concept\":\"Remaining ELF header + program-header facts as fields: e_flags, os_abi, abi_version, e_phnum/e_shnum/e_shstrndx, segments list (p_type order), interpreter, GNU_STACK/RELRO/PIE/static booleans\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Backfills so far asked elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, section_names, symbols, has_symtab. Next cheap carry-over ids: `segments`/`program_headers` (JSON of p_type names readelf-style `LOAD`/`PT_LOAD`? both recorded), `segment_count`, `section_count` (incl. NULL), `interpreter` (`/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2`), `os_abi` (`UNIX - System V` vs `ELFOSABI_SYSV` vs 0), `is_pie`/`is_static`/`has_nx`/`relro` (`full`/`partial`/`none`), `e_flags` hex. Implement in the solver facts dict (lib.binary helper) with GM-style spellings mirroring the confirmed ones (ET_EXEC style for enums, lowercase 0x hex, decimal counts). Tests: cached day01-day17 ELF members + readelf parity.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ada-gnat-deep-facts\",\"concept\":\"Ada/GNAT facts for the d17 group when its own theme is backfilled: GNAT version, binder/elaboration symbols, Ada subprogram names, decoder function, exception ids\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D17 prompt ('recover the reversible decoder') was unasked; the D17 backfill pattern means d17 facts get asked within days. From the cached Ada ELF (single_solve/work/extracted d17 member): gnat_version (`GNAT Version: 14.2.0` -> `14.2.0`), has_gnat_runtime (`__gnat_`/`ada__`/`system__`), main/binder symbols (`_ada_<main>`, `adainit`, `adafinal`, `__gnat_main`?), Ada-encoded names `pkg__sub` -> `pkg.sub` (keep mangled when asked for symbols), DWARF producer `GNU Ada 14.2.0` / DW_LANG_Ada95/2005, decoder routine name (function whose code xrefs the blob VA, via decoder-routine-locator) and its xor immediate (== header key?). Return none/false on absence; never raise.\"},\n {\"id\":\"fortran-gfortran-member\",\"concept\":\"Fortran (gfortran) ELF as a new-day member: identity cues, facts, HCFG in a COMMON block / module data / DATA statement\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Language order so far skipped Fortran/COBOL/Haskell/OCaml; Fortran is the cheapest for organizers after Ada (gcc front-end, dynamic glibc like D17). Cues: `libgfortran.so.5` NEEDED, `_gfortran_` imports, `MAIN__`, `__<module>_MOD_<name>` symbols, `GNU Fortran` DWARF producer. HCFG likely RAW in `.data`/`.rodata` (-> hcfg_storage raw_const_array). gfortran is NOT installed: `apt install gfortran` for fixtures if allowed, else hand-craft symbol/NEEDED shapes on a C ELF; targets = format elf, architecture x86-64, has_gfortran_runtime true, module procedure names demangled `module::name` vs mangled kept.\"},\n {\"id\":\"haskell-ghc-member\",\"concept\":\"Haskell (GHC) static ELF: z-encoded closures, rts strings, HCFG as a ByteString literal (raw or base64) possibly split across closures\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cues: `hs_main`, `ghczmprim_GHCziTypes_`, `base_GHCziBase_` z-encoding (zi = '.', zm = '-'), `GHC 9.x` rts banner, huge static binary, `.data` closures. Facts: has_ghc_runtime, z-decoded module names, ghc_version. Risk: a Text literal may be UTF-16 or chunked -> hcfg_scan utf16 + split modes. ghc not installed (apt ghc is ~1 GB): hand-craft fixtures with z-encoded symbol tables on a C ELF and a split-literal blob.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ocaml-native-member\",\"concept\":\"OCaml native ELF (ocamlopt): caml symbols, string literals with OCaml block headers, HCFG offset convention\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cues: `caml_startup`, `caml_main`, `camlStdlib__`, `camlDune__exe__Main`, `OCAMLRUNPARAM`. OCaml strings are header-prefixed blocks (word header + padded bytes, last byte = pad count) -> HCFG raw starts at the block payload (offset = the `H`, like D12/D14). Facts: has_ocaml_runtime, module names `camlMain__entry`. ocaml not installed: synthesize a C ELF with OCaml-shaped symbols + a block-wrapped blob.\"},\n {\"id\":\"kotlin-native-member\",\"concept\":\"Kotlin/Native ELF (konanc): `kfun:` symbols, Konan runtime, HCFG in an object literal\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Kotlin already appeared as a jar (D7); a native build is a plausible 'pair the language with a new container' twist. Cues: `kfun:` / `kclass:` / `ktype:` symbols, `Konan_main`, `Kotlin_` runtime, `kotlin.native.internal`. Strings are UTF-16 in KString objects -> hcfg_scan utf16 path + offset = first stored byte (speculative). Facts: has_kotlin_native_runtime, kfun names. Fixture: C ELF with those symbol names + UTF-16LE base64 blob.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pe-optional-header-facts\",\"concept\":\"PE/COFF facts for the PE members (d02 MinGW, d03 .NET, d10 Zig PE, d04 Go .exe): subsystem, image_base, timestamp, characteristics, dll_characteristics, section names (NUL-trimmed), entry RVA/VA, imports\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"PE members re-roll into Mastery for d02/d04/d10; a backfill on them would ask the ELF-equivalent fields: format pe, machine, entry_point (ImageBase+AddressOfEntryPoint as 0x hex?), section_names (PE names, `/4` long names resolved via COFF string table), subsystem (`console`/`IMAGE_SUBSYSTEM_WINDOWS_CUI`/3), image_base, has_symtab (COFF symbol table present), timestamp (decimal). pefile installed. Tests: cached MinGW/Zig/Go/.NET PE members from day02-day16 artifacts + record both spelling families.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cobol-gnucobol-member\",\"concept\":\"GnuCOBOL ELF (cobc): libcob NEEDED, cob_init, PIC X working-storage holding the HCFG\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cues: `libcob.so.4` NEEDED, `cob_init`/`cob_module_enter`, `GnuCOBOL` strings, program-id symbols upper-case. WORKING-STORAGE `PIC X(n) VALUE` literals sit raw in `.data` (-> raw_const_array) but COBOL source limits literal length (~160 chars) so the blob may be SPLIT across consecutive fields -> hcfg_scan split mode. Facts: has_cobol_runtime, program_id. gnucobol not installed: synthesize.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dart-aot-snapshot\",\"concept\":\"Dart AOT executable (`dart compile exe`): snapshot sections, HCFG inside the isolate snapshot (possibly compressed/obfuscated)\",\"priority\":3,\"